          "source": "palm",
          "verdict": "benign",
          "analysis": "The analyzed binary is a legitimate Windows system utility known as the Filter Manager Control Program (fltmc.exe). Its functionality is centered around managing file system mini-filter drivers using the FltLib library. Key behaviors observed in the decompilation include the ability to load/unload filters (FilterLoad, FilterUnload), attach/detach filter instances (FilterAttach, FilterDetach), and enumerate volumes and filter metadata (FilterVolumeFindFirst, FilterInstanceFindFirst). The sample correctly implements privilege escalation for administrative tasks, specifically requesting SeLoadDriverPrivilege via AdjustTokenPrivileges. No malicious patterns, suspicious strings, or unauthorized behaviors were detected; it is a standard administrative tool.",
          "category": "code_insight",
          "id": "8099107e5bfbed1cb819e4477e1ad84e01397f215e9255b2616bb4793d6490be-file-palm"
        }
